"The art'h old house is a historic ritual site on Rapport I, tens of miles from the siblinghold."
"It is a cluster of buildings the size of a resort hotel, glimmering with iridescence."
"Nobody lives there; keeping it habitable would take impractical wizard labor."
"Some things an art'h can only do at the old house."
"It has no windows, only openings where spells once let good weather in; some rooms lack roofs."
"Its grand hall has columns carved as plants and animals over a glossy leaf-strewn floor."
"A spell court of stone stars lies under the leaves; dirt there leaves no stains."
"The old house drinks visitors' blood."
"Old terraced gardens, a farewell path and a sap well surround it, near a ruined knight school."
"Vines with peach-throated white flowers there smell like baked bread; the grass is bluish green."
